{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766981,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"amber_un","paid":0,"title":"Sparkathon 2.0","festival_id":519255,"organization_id":13183,"web_url":"www.concetto.in\/events","start_date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-10T13:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/sparkathon-20-indian-institute-of-technology-indian-school-of-mines-iit-ism-dhanbad-1766981","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Sparkathon 2.0 &ndash; The Electronics Ideathon:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Official Rulebook:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Sparkathon 2.0 is an electronics-focused ideathon that challenges students to develop original, innovative, and technically sound solutions to real-world problems.<\/p>\n<p>The event consists of two rounds:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Preliminary Individual Quiz<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Final Ideation, Presentation &amp; Evaluation<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Round 1:<\/strong> Preliminary Quiz &mdash; Top 12 Teams<\/li>\n<li><strong>Round 2:<\/strong> Problem Allocation &mdash; Lottery System<\/li>\n<li><strong>Round 2:<\/strong> Ideation &amp; PPT Preparation &mdash; 90 Minutes<\/li>\n<li><strong>Round 2:<\/strong> Presentation + Q&amp;A &mdash; 15 Minutes\/Team<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility &amp; Team Specifications:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to students from all branches.<\/li>\n<li>Team size: 2&ndash;4 members.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must have a unique team name.<\/li>\n<li>A participant may be part of only one team.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must remain unchanged throughout the event.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Round 1 &ndash; Preliminary Quiz:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The quiz will be conducted individually; it will not be team-wise.<\/li>\n<li>Every team member must attempt the quiz independently.<\/li>\n<li>Duration: <strong>30 minutes<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Questions will cover fundamental technical concepts related to electronics and the domains relevant to the final problem statements.<\/li>\n<li>Collaboration or discussion between team members during the quiz is not permitted.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Team Score:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The team's Round 1 score will be the average of the individual scores of all its members.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Team Score = Sum of individual scores &divide; Number of team members<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The top 12 teams based on this score will qualify for Round 2.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 2 &ndash; Problem Statement Allocation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Two final problem statements will be provided:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Problem Statement 1<\/strong><\/li>\n<li><strong>Problem Statement 2<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>The qualified teams will be assigned a problem statement through a lottery\/chit system.<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be ranked according to their Round 1 scores.<\/li>\n<li>The lottery will begin with the highest-ranked team and proceed in descending order.<\/li>\n<li>Each team will randomly draw a chit to determine its assigned problem statement.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must develop their solution exclusively for the problem statement assigned to them.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Preparation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Qualified teams will receive <strong>90 minutes<\/strong> to develop their solution and prepare their presentation.<\/p>\n<p>The solution must be conceived and developed during this preparation period.<\/p>\n<p>Internet access is permitted for research, references, datasheets and technical information, but copying complete existing solutions or presentations is strictly prohibited.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Presentation:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Each team may use a maximum of <strong>6 slides<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p>The presentation should effectively cover:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team &amp; Problem Statement<\/li>\n<li>Problem Understanding<\/li>\n<li>Proposed Solution &amp; Innovation<\/li>\n<li>Technical Approach \/ Block Diagram<\/li>\n<li>Feasibility &amp; Practical Impact<\/li>\n<li>Conclusion \/ Future Scope<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Teams may modify the structure as appropriate to their solution.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Presentation Time:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Maximum <strong>15 minutes per team<\/strong>:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Presentation:<\/strong> 10 minutes<\/li>\n<li><strong>Q&amp;A:<\/strong> 5 minutes<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Teams are expected to manage the allotted time effectively.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Creativity, Originality &amp; Innovation &mdash; 25<\/li>\n<li>Understanding of the Problem &mdash; 20<\/li>\n<li>Technical Feasibility &amp; Approach &mdash; 20<\/li>\n<li>PPT Content &amp; Quality &mdash; 15<\/li>\n<li>Presentation &amp; Communication &mdash; 10<\/li>\n<li>Handling of Questions \/ Q&amp;A &mdash; 10<\/li>\n<li><strong>Total &mdash; 100<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Judges will consider the uniqueness of the idea, quality of the proposed solution, technical reasoning, clarity of the PPT, presentation style, team coordination, and ability to handle questions.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must consist of 2&ndash;4 members.<\/li>\n<li>Round 1 must be attempted individually by every team member.<\/li>\n<li>Team scores in Round 1 will be calculated using the average individual score.<\/li>\n<li>The top 12 teams will qualify for Round 2.<\/li>\n<li>Problem statements will be assigned through the lottery system based on Round 1 ranking.<\/li>\n<li>Teams will have 90 minutes to prepare their solution and presentation.<\/li>\n<li>The presentation must not exceed 6 slides.<\/li>\n<li>The complete presentation and Q&amp;A must not exceed 15 minutes.<\/li>\n<li>Solutions must be original and innovative.<\/li>\n<li>Internet use is permitted for research but not for copying complete solutions.<\/li>\n<li>Plagiarism, cheating, deliberate copying, or misconduct may result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Judges' decisions regarding evaluation and results will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>The organisers reserve the right to make necessary changes to the event schedule or rules.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Winner &ndash; Problem Statement 1 &mdash; \u20b95,000<\/li>\n<li>Winner &ndash; Problem Statement 2 &mdash; \u20b95,000<\/li>\n<li><strong>Total Prize Pool &mdash; \u20b910,000<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>General Instructions:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The event will be conducted offline.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must report at the designated venue on time.<\/li>\n<li>Valid college identification may be required.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must maintain discipline and follow instructions from the organisers.<\/li>\n<li>Any changes to the schedule will be communicated by the organising team.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Think Different. Build Original. Present Bold.<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":19183409,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-07T03:50:29+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T18:54:56+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"IkEMOhX","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":0,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":7,"checked":null,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":11,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-07 17:19:54","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_s